  "findings": [
    "Settings originally hid GitHub controls after failed integration reads and had no account-link OAuth action in Sign-in methods.",
    "The legacy GET /integrations projection discarded githubAccess, so reauthorization_required looked like an absent repository installation.",
    "Browser callback failures originally exposed JSON with no recovery page; an installation popup could display completion copy for an error.",
    "GITHUB_IDENTITY_CONFLICT correctly protects existing numeric GitHub identity bindings. Actual cookie actors are used throughout shared-ledger flows; ledger Admin roles confer no provider repository permissions."
  ],
  "changes": [
    "Confirmed session accounts can connect/reconnect their own GitHub identity with intent=link independently of integration-read availability.",
    "GET /integrations preserves top-level githubAccess while retaining the existing compatible DTO and read-only contract.",
    "Explicit reauthorization_required directs account reconnect before installation; unknown/transient failures do not claim disconnected accounts or successful repository counts.",
    "Exact account and installation callbacks redirect HTML JSON errors to fixed same-origin recovery destinations, bounded to 4KiB and allowlisted codes. OAuth code/state/provider parameters are not copied.",
    "Recovery screens preserve the JSON API contract, cookies, identity protection and popup/session fences; failure popups neither synchronize nor claim success."
  ],
